.TH TUIPLAYER 1 "2026-11-07" "tuiplayer 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuiplayer \- barebones keyboard-driven TUI music player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuiplayer
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtuiplayer\fR is a barebones, single-file terminal music player.
A search races several free public sources (Piped and Invidious
instances) concurrently and plays the first response through
.BR mpv (1).
\fByt-dlp\fR(1) is used for stream resolution and as the guaranteed
playback fallback.
.PP
After a track starts playing, the next track is silently buffered in a
muted mpv session; selecting it later starts playback almost instantly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B tab
Toggle focus between the search box and the result list.
.TP
.BR enter
Search (search box) or play the selected track and prefetch the next
one (result list).
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k
Move the selection.
.TP
.B s
Stop playback.
.TP
.B n
Play the next track.
.TP
.BR q ", " esc
Quit. \fBesc\fR first clears the search box when focused.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR python , \  mpv (1), \ yt-dlp (1)
.SH FILES
No configuration; tweak the constants inside \fI/usr/bin/tuiplayer\fR.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exits with a message on stderr if \fBmpv\fR or \fByt-dlp\fR is missing.
Search failures are reported in the status line; playback falls back
through direct URL, yt-dlp URL, and the yt-dlp\ ->\ mpv pipe.
